<title>BRAZIL: MOTOR RACING-BRAZILIAN GRAND PRIX PRACTICE TIMES.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-BRAZILIAN GRAND PRIX PRACTICE TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times after Friday's opening practice for Sunday's Brazilian Grand Prix motor race:</p>
<p>1. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) Williams one minute  17.506 seconds</p>
<p>2. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada) Williams 1:17.829</p>
<p>3. Jean Alesi (France) Benetton 1:18.000</p>
<p>4. Johnny Herbert (Britain) Sauber 1:18.261</p>
<p>5. Gerhard Berger (Austria) Benetton 1:18.437</p>
<p>6. Ralf Schumacher (Germany) Jordan 1:18.479</p>
<p>7. Michael Schumacher (Germany) Ferrari 1:18.488</p>
<p>8. David Coulthard (Britain) McLaren 1:18.818</p>
<p>9. Damon Hill (Britain) Arrows 1:18.978</p>
<p>10. Mika Hakkinen (Finland) McLaren 1:19.271</p>
<p>11. Ginacarlo Fisichella (Italy) Jordan 1:19.326</p>
<p>12. Olivier Panis (France) Prost 1:19.408.</p>
</text>
